From 61e0f969ac7d324436fcbee7d1f3e4312afa8ccb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Jeffery <andrew@codeconstruct.com.au>
Date: Wed, 17 Dec 2025 11:58:48 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] Revert "mtd: spi-nor: macronix: Drop the redundant flash info
 fields"

This reverts commit 947c86e481a027ed5948434096e506f307bd7114.

Unfortunately, booting QEMU's ast2600-evb with 947c86e481a0 ("mtd:
spi-nor: macronix: Drop the redundant flash info fields") fails as
the MTD drivers fail to bind. Instead, they report:

   BFPT parsing failed. Please consider using SPI_NOR_SKIP_SFDP when declaring the flash

The failure does not occur on equivalent hardware. Reverting the change
yields a successful boot in both environments, so do that while we track
down the deficiency in QEMU.

Signed-off-by: Andrew Jeffery <andrew@codeconstruct.com.au>
---
 drivers/mtd/spi-nor/macronix.c | 36 +++++++++++++++++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

